node_modules/
dist/
build/

# ── Environment files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DENY-BY-DEFAULT. This block was previously a hand-maintained list
# (.env, .env.local, .env.production) which did not cover new variants — that
# gap is how server/.env.development reached a public commit carrying a live
# MongoDB Atlas credential.
#
# The rule is now pattern-based: ANYTHING starting with `.env` is ignored at any
# depth — `.env`, `.env.staging`, and even a typo'd `.envlocal` (which a
# `.env.*` rule would miss, and which is already present in this repo). Only
# explicitly-safe template files are allowed back in. Adding a new environment
# needs no change here and cannot be committed by accident.
#
# If you add a genuinely public template, whitelist it explicitly below —
# never loosen the deny rules above it.
.env*
**/.env*

# Safe templates: shape only, no real values. Keep this list short.
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
!.env.sample
!**/.env.sample
!.env.template
!**/.env.template

*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/worktrees/
coverage/
deploy/certs/
deploy/certbot-www/
